            <description><![CDATA[<style>
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 197)</h2>
<p><b>You can see each other work.</b> In a shared review, the pen shows as it moves and everyone's pointer is visible — each in their own colour, with their name on it.</p>
<ul>
<li>In a room you can point at the frame and say "that edge". Over a connection you can't, and this is what closes that gap.</li>
<li><b>Live only.</b> Pointers and half-drawn strokes are never saved — the finished mark arrives separately and is stored like any other annotation.</li>
<li>A reviewer who drops out doesn't leave a pointer behind implying they're still looking.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Everyone should update together.</b> This build speaks a newer sync protocol, so a shared review needs all participants on build 197 or later. An older copy is now told to update, rather than being disconnected without explanation as it would have been before.</p>
]]></description>
